# Build context of the backend / celery image (docker/backend.Dockerfile, context apps/backend).
# The repo-root .dockerignore does NOT apply here (it is a different build context), so without this file the
# image carried a 200 MB virtualenv, a 35 MB production data dump, the .env file with secrets and stray uploads.
# Patterns without a leading ** match the backend folder's top level only.

# local Python environments and caches
venv/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# secrets: the server passes them at run time (env_file / bind mount), they must never be baked into an image
.env
.env.*

# data dumps, spreadsheets and photos lying around the backend folder (not used by the running code)
*.json
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.jpg
*.png
error.html
purchase_invoices/
media/
staticfiles/
logs/
*.log
*.dump
*.sqlite3

# the GST Excel templates ARE needed at run time (apps/reports/exports read resources/gst_templates)
!resources/
